### Actions and the Long-Press Menu
`actions` chooses the toolbar's and the menu's actions and their order, and calling `preventDefault()` in the `action` event leaves one to the host; with `contextMenu` set to `false`, a long press or a right-click no longer opens the menu.

```vue
<script setup lang="ts">
import type { ImagePreviewActionEvent } from '@talex-touch/tuffex/image-preview'

function onAction(event: ImagePreviewActionEvent) {
  // The host saves into its own album instead; the preview leaves it alone
  if (event.action === 'download') {
    event.preventDefault()
    saveToAlbum(event.item.url)
  }
}
</script>

<template>
  <TxImagePreview
    v-model:open="open"
    :images="images"
    :actions="['rotate', 'copy', 'download']"
    @action="onAction"
  />
</template>
```

### Materials and the Strip
`indicator` picks a strip of thumbnails, dots, or nothing, `maskSurface` / `controlSurface` pick the materials behind the image and under the controls, and `bounce` sets how far pages, jumps, and the flight overshoot.
